eta + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1\\):\n\n\\[\nD = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\cos^2 \\alpha & \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\alpha & \\sin^2 \\alpha \\\\\n\\cos^2 \\beta & \\cos \\beta \\sin \\beta & \\sin^2 \\beta \\\\\n\\cos^2 \\gamma & \\cos \\gamma \\sin \\gamma & \\sin^2 \\gamma \\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the determinant for such matrices, we know it's an identity matrix determinant. Let's confirm by recognizing that the elements under the equation ( i.e. c rows and elements under column 3) sum to 3 when \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi\\). Thus, \\(D = \\begin{vmatrix}\n1 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 1 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 0 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = 1\\).\n\nSo, using the properties of determinants and verifying the solution from the identity matrix. \n\nThus, the value of the determinant is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0}\n\\]",
